    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="1603" n="1452" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v07-09mSupp/pg1452"/>

                <head>330. Memorandum from McNamara to
                        Rusk, July 3<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d330-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-07-03">July 3, 1963</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d330-01" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d330-01"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Balance of Payments</item>
                </list>
                <p>In a memorandum dated April 20, 1963 to the Cabinet Committee on the Balance of
                    Payments, the President requested that I submit recommendations on specific
                    actions which could be completed by the end of 1964 with a target of a gross
                    reduction in the annual rate of Department of Defense expenditures abroad of
                    $300–400 million below FY 1963 levels.</p>
                <p>A draft memorandum to the President in response to his request is attached.</p>
                <p>May I have your comments on the course of action recommended in the
                    memorandum.</p>
                <closer><signed>Robert S.
                    McNamara</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d330-a1.xml" xpointer="d330-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
                <p>Solicits Department of State comments on attached memorandum to the President
                    regarding DOD actions to reduce expenditures
                    abroad. Secret. 10 pp. Department of State, Central Files, FN 12 US.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
